migration:
  title: Tier-3 pipeline rearchitecture - REST poll to KiteTicker WebSocket, event-driven, edge-triggered
  goal: Replace the 5s REST-polling / DB-hop / level-triggered signal->execution pipeline with a push-based WebSocket feed, in-process event-driven evaluation, edge-triggered execution, write-behind audit persistence, and tick-driven position monitoring backed by exchange-side stop orders.
  endState: Kite ticks (LTP/OI/volume) push into tier3-signal buffer; evaluator runs in-process on relevant ticks; orders fire only on state transitions with cooldown + per-user position state machine; Postgres is an async write-behind audit log; position monitor evaluates ratchet on every tick and places an exchange-side SL backstop.
  reason: A 5s poll adds latency and cost. Exit latency is where a poll costs real money. The DB hop and level-triggered scan produced stale-signal windows and re-entry churn (20 trades from one direction). Push + edge-trigger + in-process eval removes latency, churn, and naked-position risk.
  lastUpdated: 2026-07-05

requirements[5]{id,title,detail,touches}:
  R1,WebSocket feed,"Replace Tier-3 REST poll with KiteTicker WebSocket. Subscribe ~60 option tokens + NIFTY spot in full mode. Push LTP/OI/volume on change instead of 5s pull. tier3-signal.ts stays pure math on rolling buffer - fed by tick handler instead of timer. Recompute IV/gamma/PCR/maxPain (Newton-Raphson, sub-ms for 60 instruments) on each relevant tick.","tier3 fetch/poll path; kite-option-chain feed source; tier3-refresh scheduler loop"
  R2,In-process context,"Kill the DB hop between signal and executor. Tick handler calls evaluator directly (or in-process EventEmitter for decoupling). Slow inputs - ensemble direction, HMM regime, FlipGuard, session priors - live in a single versioned in-memory context object updated atomically by the 5-min scheduler (build new object, swap reference). Hot path reads with zero locking.","signal-executor read path; scheduler context publishing; snapshot read-before-execute"
  R3,Edge-triggered execution,"Make execution edge-triggered not level-triggered. Fire only on state transitions (NONE->CALL, CALL->PUT) with cooldown and explicit per-user position-state machine. Kills the 30-min stale-signal window and re-entry churn.","signal-executor scanAndExecutePendingSignals; per-user processing/dedup; position state tracking"
  R4,Write-behind audit,"Demote Postgres to write-behind audit log. Every snapshot, signal event, execution still persisted (needed for Resolution scheduler + analytics) but via async fire-and-forget queue that never blocks tick->order chain. Drop material-change gating on signal path; keep it only as optional persistence-volume optimization.","snapshot persistence; signal_executions writes; material-change gate; async queue"
  R5,Tick-driven exits + exchange SL,"Position monitor goes tick-driven, evaluating ratchet stop on every tick of held instruments. Place exchange-side SL order at hard-stop level as backstop so a dead process never leaves a naked position. Highest-value fix - exit latency is where 5s poll costs money.","position-monitor monitorOpenPositions; ratchet compute; exit order path; exchange SL placement"

decisions:
  rollout: DIRECT_REPLACEMENT
  rolloutNote: Replace the polling path outright, no feature flag. Fastest, highest risk on live-money system - user accepted.
  sequencing: INFRA_FIRST_DEPENDENCY_ORDER
  sequencingNote: WebSocket feed -> in-memory context -> edge-triggered exec -> write-behind audit -> tick-driven exits + exchange SL. Each batch builds on the previous.

constraints:
  noTouchRule: Anything NOT explicitly named in the 5 requirements stays untouched.
  preserved[6]:
    - Ensemble / HMM / market-agent slow-path logic (only HOW it publishes to hot path changes, per R2)
    - tier3-signal.ts pure-math engine (only its INPUT source changes from timer to tick, per R1)
    - DB table/column shapes (only WHEN/HOW rows are written changes, per R4)
    - News ingestion / Neo4j story graph / ChromaDB (out of scope)
    - Resolution scheduler and analytics consumers of persisted rows (must keep working, per R4)
    - Token refresh scheduler (6h Kite token refresh) unless WebSocket auth requires it

dependencies:
  external[4]{name,impact}:
    KiteTicker WebSocket,"New dependency - KiteConnect ticker API. Auth via api_key + access_token. Subscribe/setMode(full) for OI+volume. Reconnect handling required."
    Kite Connect REST,"Still used for order placement, positions, instrument list, token->symbol resolution. Not removed."
    Postgres/Drizzle,"Becomes async write target. Resolution scheduler + analytics read from same tables - shapes must not change."
    Single Node process,"Whole design assumes one process - enables in-memory context + direct evaluator calls. No horizontal scaling assumed."
  downstream[3]:
    - Resolution scheduler (24h) marks snapshots correct/incorrect - depends on snapshot rows still being written
    - Frontend trading UI (routes/trading.ts) reads market-data/active-trades/history - must keep returning data
    - signal_executions rows feed P&L analytics

timeline:
  priorityOrder: R1, R2, R3, R4, R5
  batching: 5-10 files per batch, one requirement cluster at a time, git tag rollback point per batch
  criticalRisk: Live-money execution path. Direct replacement means old poll path is removed - must verify order placement + exit paths before market open on deploy day.
